  "summary": "BLISTER is a novel loader that uses valid code-signing certificates to evade detection. It is typically dropped as a DLL, executed by rundll32.exe, and establishes persistence via the user's Startup folder. The loader decodes and injects second-stage payloads like Cobalt Strike or BitRat into memory, often into a WerFault.exe process.",
